{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>The men of Anathoth.</b> It is written of them: \"Thus said YHWH: the young men shall die by the sword, their sons and their daughters shall die by famine, and there shall be no remnant left to them, for I will bring evil upon the men of Anathoth in the year of their punishment.\" Yet from tradition we know that they returned to El before the day of reckoning, and the decree was annulled from upon them, and one hundred twenty-eight of them remained."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The quoted passage alludes to Jeremiah 11:21–23 and 29:18–19; Ibn Ezra paraphrases loosely. The phrase שנת פקדתם (\"in the year of their punishment\") appears to be Ibn Ezra's own compressed framing rather than a direct citation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:41:54.639935376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}